     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: All project activities including civil construction and system installation are progressing at a good pace. The project is on schedule and expected to be completed by June 2025. Out of 82 km of RRTS corridor, 55km section from New Ashok Nagar to Meerut South is operational. Overall physical progress is 80% till 30 September 2024.Multimodal integration of RRTS with various modes has been planned and under implementation.

Anand Vihar RRTS Station and Ghaziabad RRTS station has been completed and opened to public.BIM Lab has been established and is in operation at the Admin Building at Duhai Depot.

Gender-friendly workplace policy is beeing developed and institutionalized within the NCRTC.816 personnel of NCRTC attended training programs organized by ADB on project and contract management, financial management, procurement, safeguards and gender etc.

NCRTC has engaged and mobilized consultants to conduct need analysis and training for employment and/ entrepreneurial opportunities. Analysis of employment opportunities and training needs identification completed.Training programs for employment and/or entrepreneurial opportunities are being implemented.

NCRTC to identify the beneficiaries and distribution of assistive aids. Persons with disability list of all 1,000 beneficiaries has been identified and in process for approval. Procurement of assistive aids will commence, following approval of list of beneficiaries.EWCD-friendly and climate- and disaster resilient features have been built into the project design.6 coaches have provision of 4 CCTV cameras per coach.Delhi-Meerut RRTS project is currently under implementation.</narrative>
